[{:db/id 17592186172089 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7aa4e4d5-0080-5cb6-bebe-9d6c94950127" "question-fb00dc0e-66fe-5382-b23d-00ac1fa661b6" "question-70661cc4-274a-5311-99fc-fa9cf5ff480d" "question-586f6a61-ad62-56e5-9a2c-611ea0a2819c" "question-8c80223d-79b2-5d97-8d88-3fa6275a012a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172090 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-64433fed-4bfa-5173-80b1-78dbdf657823" "question-202a66ff-7a74-5355-8081-a73c26b6f2c0" "question-1b5a0004-da97-5a43-bf86-5bd3413d5383" "question-6947d1ad-4cd9-585a-b94f-f141875b9f2d" "question-27eda322-b707-5345-adf8-0465217fdeaf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7aa4e4d5-0080-5cb6-bebe-9d6c94950127" :question/id #uuid "7aa4e4d5-0080-5cb6-bebe-9d6c94950127" :question/math-academy-id "q-123511" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r={sin}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi $ ?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={sin}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=3{sin}^{2}\\,\\theta \\text{ }\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{({sin}^{3}\\,\\theta )}^{2}+{(3{sin}^{2}\\,\\theta \\text{ }\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{sin}^{6}\\,\\theta +9{sin}^{4}\\,\\theta \\text{ }\\,{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}\\,\\theta \\sqrt{{sin}^{2}\\,\\theta +9{cos}^{2}\\,\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}\\,\\theta \\sqrt{1+8{cos}^{2}\\,\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ce35695c-d7ed-5650-b6f0-c0d7e8432851"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ce35695c-d7ed-5650-b6f0-c0d7e8432851" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce35695c-d7ed-5650-b6f0-c0d7e8432851" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3795af39-24b8-5073-90c3-faa50ef95682" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4d4c2c76-9822-5adf-bfb2-5991320c3105" "answer-8c59bfa2-430e-5926-995c-ce492668dd20" "answer-3795af39-24b8-5073-90c3-faa50ef95682" "answer-9d63f17c-0ef7-5244-bb03-4939eb982145" "answer-26a04d3a-0123-57f0-b050-a4cee7844a9d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d4c2c76-9822-5adf-bfb2-5991320c3105" :answer/id #uuid "4d4c2c76-9822-5adf-bfb2-5991320c3105" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }sin\\,\\theta \\sqrt{1+6{cos}^{2}\\,\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c59bfa2-430e-5926-995c-ce492668dd20" :answer/id #uuid "8c59bfa2-430e-5926-995c-ce492668dd20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }sin\\,\\theta \\sqrt{1-8{sin}^{2}\\,\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3795af39-24b8-5073-90c3-faa50ef95682" :answer/id #uuid "3795af39-24b8-5073-90c3-faa50ef95682" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}\\,\\theta \\sqrt{1+8{cos}^{2}\\,\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d63f17c-0ef7-5244-bb03-4939eb982145" :answer/id #uuid "9d63f17c-0ef7-5244-bb03-4939eb982145" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}\\,\\theta \\sqrt{4+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26a04d3a-0123-57f0-b050-a4cee7844a9d" :answer/id #uuid "26a04d3a-0123-57f0-b050-a4cee7844a9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{3}\\,\\theta \\sqrt{1+9{cos}^{2}\\,\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fb00dc0e-66fe-5382-b23d-00ac1fa661b6" :question/id #uuid "fb00dc0e-66fe-5382-b23d-00ac1fa661b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-123559" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r={csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,$ for $\\pi /3\\le \\theta \\le \\pi /2?$" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-3{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{({csc}^{3}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(-3{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{csc}^{6}⁡\\theta +9{csc}^{6}⁡\\theta {cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{csc}^{6}⁡\\theta (1+9{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta })\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+9{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f8dcb75d-dac3-5c81-8f6e-1e4763779208"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f8dcb75d-dac3-5c81-8f6e-1e4763779208" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8dcb75d-dac3-5c81-8f6e-1e4763779208" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-369bbef4-e31e-5ef6-9afb-de7d3e21d28f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-39da32fb-4fd3-56f4-8b48-27bfa06dac2a" "answer-ba9bc000-67c4-53d2-b325-fa53d6ea89eb" "answer-7d101eaf-b053-5e48-a386-fa7d17ca7d49" "answer-0d2aeb4a-6148-5344-8241-a30ca0414bf3" "answer-369bbef4-e31e-5ef6-9afb-de7d3e21d28f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39da32fb-4fd3-56f4-8b48-27bfa06dac2a" :answer/id #uuid "39da32fb-4fd3-56f4-8b48-27bfa06dac2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+8{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba9bc000-67c4-53d2-b325-fa53d6ea89eb" :answer/id #uuid "ba9bc000-67c4-53d2-b325-fa53d6ea89eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+7{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d101eaf-b053-5e48-a386-fa7d17ca7d49" :answer/id #uuid "7d101eaf-b053-5e48-a386-fa7d17ca7d49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{5+4{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d2aeb4a-6148-5344-8241-a30ca0414bf3" :answer/id #uuid "0d2aeb4a-6148-5344-8241-a30ca0414bf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+5{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-369bbef4-e31e-5ef6-9afb-de7d3e21d28f" :answer/id #uuid "369bbef4-e31e-5ef6-9afb-de7d3e21d28f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{3}⁡\\theta \\sqrt{1+9{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-70661cc4-274a-5311-99fc-fa9cf5ff480d" :question/id #uuid "70661cc4-274a-5311-99fc-fa9cf5ff480d" :question/math-academy-id "q-123426" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=2{cos}^{3}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3})\\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le 3\\pi $ ?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2{cos}^{3}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3})\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-2{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }\\sqrt{{(2{cos}^{3}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3}))}^{2}+{(-2{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3}))}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }\\sqrt{{cos}^{6}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3})+{cos}^{4}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3}){sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3})}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3})\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3})}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3})\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c16bafac-0287-5357-8266-d49db38ec2b3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c16bafac-0287-5357-8266-d49db38ec2b3" :answer-field/id #uuid "c16bafac-0287-5357-8266-d49db38ec2b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-76d06d75-8601-5c9f-931a-e187e9f7e576" :answer-field/choices ["answer-36dfca93-7965-545e-ae64-ea4e15350f14" "answer-76d06d75-8601-5c9f-931a-e187e9f7e576" "answer-6b63604b-d8a6-599a-838b-2b74c3f0610a" "answer-8e346b38-71c5-5bc3-bda7-aa1f806c4b1f" "answer-b38cf43c-b624-53ab-921c-a21f0a6ea62f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36dfca93-7965-545e-ae64-ea4e15350f14" :answer/id #uuid "36dfca93-7965-545e-ae64-ea4e15350f14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3})\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76d06d75-8601-5c9f-931a-e187e9f7e576" :answer/id #uuid "76d06d75-8601-5c9f-931a-e187e9f7e576" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3})\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b63604b-d8a6-599a-838b-2b74c3f0610a" :answer/id #uuid "6b63604b-d8a6-599a-838b-2b74c3f0610a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3})\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e346b38-71c5-5bc3-bda7-aa1f806c4b1f" :answer/id #uuid "8e346b38-71c5-5bc3-bda7-aa1f806c4b1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3})\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b38cf43c-b624-53ab-921c-a21f0a6ea62f" :answer/id #uuid "b38cf43c-b624-53ab-921c-a21f0a6ea62f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{3})\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-586f6a61-ad62-56e5-9a2c-611ea0a2819c" :question/id #uuid "586f6a61-ad62-56e5-9a2c-611ea0a2819c" :question/math-academy-id "q-123379" :question/problem "![](images/19/19725cfd8068973c899fcb4f54abcebbbfcd24bd68aec510b9d41cee2c2cd02a.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=2-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,$ for $\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=2-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(2-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +16{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +16{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +16}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{20-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1cca78f2-2d1d-5264-9180-c7409ad32bd4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1cca78f2-2d1d-5264-9180-c7409ad32bd4" :answer-field/id #uuid "1cca78f2-2d1d-5264-9180-c7409ad32bd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-392cdecf-382d-5eaf-8512-13e93f090b11" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fdef13fa-c9e2-5073-8dc0-04da2e76ab8c" "answer-392cdecf-382d-5eaf-8512-13e93f090b11" "answer-bb292c1a-79be-51a1-91b7-2783d7d709cb" "answer-17652adb-f0bd-5e06-b55e-fb60b41d8171" "answer-e84048f5-bc2b-5cb4-a79e-ebf71a21e3cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdef13fa-c9e2-5073-8dc0-04da2e76ab8c" :answer/id #uuid "fdef13fa-c9e2-5073-8dc0-04da2e76ab8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-392cdecf-382d-5eaf-8512-13e93f090b11" :answer/id #uuid "392cdecf-382d-5eaf-8512-13e93f090b11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb292c1a-79be-51a1-91b7-2783d7d709cb" :answer/id #uuid "bb292c1a-79be-51a1-91b7-2783d7d709cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17652adb-f0bd-5e06-b55e-fb60b41d8171" :answer/id #uuid "17652adb-f0bd-5e06-b55e-fb60b41d8171" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{5-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e84048f5-bc2b-5cb4-a79e-ebf71a21e3cf" :answer/id #uuid "e84048f5-bc2b-5cb4-a79e-ebf71a21e3cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{8-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8c80223d-79b2-5d97-8d88-3fa6275a012a" :question/id #uuid "8c80223d-79b2-5d97-8d88-3fa6275a012a" :question/math-academy-id "q-123377" :question/problem "![](images/3b/3b8ef36c29d1babc5c3ccf1d474678a18ed5937b883e026d18d5c7ea1aaaa3f5.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=3+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta \\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=3+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expression for our line integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(3+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta )^{2}+(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta )^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡3\\theta +9{cos}^{2}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{9+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +1+8{cos}^{2}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{10+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +8{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-970ad32f-3bc8-5eae-a83f-06f38e693fb2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-970ad32f-3bc8-5eae-a83f-06f38e693fb2" :answer-field/id #uuid "970ad32f-3bc8-5eae-a83f-06f38e693fb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-609847c3-196c-5c58-9386-82fb40230109" :answer-field/choices ["answer-369565c3-561a-50ca-9be4-d934f4abc68d" "answer-1015c73e-191b-5d23-bc1d-08512f03b481" "answer-609847c3-196c-5c58-9386-82fb40230109" "answer-8a907a7b-6b1a-50eb-9d99-ac2cfde55650" "answer-0081acc5-b8a0-5432-9f86-16b58fe1f445"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-369565c3-561a-50ca-9be4-d934f4abc68d" :answer/id #uuid "369565c3-561a-50ca-9be4-d934f4abc68d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +6\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1015c73e-191b-5d23-bc1d-08512f03b481" :answer/id #uuid "1015c73e-191b-5d23-bc1d-08512f03b481" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+6{sin}^{2}⁡3\\theta +8\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-609847c3-196c-5c58-9386-82fb40230109" :answer/id #uuid "609847c3-196c-5c58-9386-82fb40230109" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{10+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +8{cos}^{2}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a907a7b-6b1a-50eb-9d99-ac2cfde55650" :answer/id #uuid "8a907a7b-6b1a-50eb-9d99-ac2cfde55650" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{10\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +9{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0081acc5-b8a0-5432-9f86-16b58fe1f445" :answer/id #uuid "0081acc5-b8a0-5432-9f86-16b58fe1f445" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{8+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\theta +10\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-64433fed-4bfa-5173-80b1-78dbdf657823" :question/id #uuid "64433fed-4bfa-5173-80b1-78dbdf657823" :question/math-academy-id "q-123588" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r={e}^{3\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r={e}^{3\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=3{e}^{3\\theta }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{({e}^{3\\theta })}^{2}+{(3{e}^{3\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{e}^{6\\theta }+9{e}^{6\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{10{e}^{6\\theta }}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{3\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{3}{e}^{3\\theta }{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{3}({e}^{3\\pi /2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1e002bc4-fe0a-5bee-a659-5aa8805e7b8d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1e002bc4-fe0a-5bee-a659-5aa8805e7b8d" :answer-field/id #uuid "1e002bc4-fe0a-5bee-a659-5aa8805e7b8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-31bfc9f7-7493-57e1-b147-3f23514daabe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8b2f9b34-0fbf-5fd5-b8c6-26a3b94bca3b" "answer-a7579eaa-09d8-506a-899e-dbfeb07bdb29" "answer-1a069d4b-132f-5a64-b073-4120e458ea69" "answer-31bfc9f7-7493-57e1-b147-3f23514daabe" "answer-df6196e6-e9fa-5643-bd76-62133f7a731d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b2f9b34-0fbf-5fd5-b8c6-26a3b94bca3b" :answer/id #uuid "8b2f9b34-0fbf-5fd5-b8c6-26a3b94bca3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10\\sqrt{3}}{3}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7579eaa-09d8-506a-899e-dbfeb07bdb29" :answer/id #uuid "a7579eaa-09d8-506a-899e-dbfeb07bdb29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a069d4b-132f-5a64-b073-4120e458ea69" :answer/id #uuid "1a069d4b-132f-5a64-b073-4120e458ea69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}({e}^{5\\pi /2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31bfc9f7-7493-57e1-b147-3f23514daabe" :answer/id #uuid "31bfc9f7-7493-57e1-b147-3f23514daabe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{3}({e}^{3\\pi /2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df6196e6-e9fa-5643-bd76-62133f7a731d" :answer/id #uuid "df6196e6-e9fa-5643-bd76-62133f7a731d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{6}({e}^{3\\pi /4}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-202a66ff-7a74-5355-8081-a73c26b6f2c0" :question/id #uuid "202a66ff-7a74-5355-8081-a73c26b6f2c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-123579" :question/problem "![](images/05/051efe86fa3f118dd82c41f32071982bcdbacbab75212d867a5a809f37506192.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1943cf7d-279c-5e8f-b1f0-69426fcd72d6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1943cf7d-279c-5e8f-b1f0-69426fcd72d6" :answer-field/id #uuid "1943cf7d-279c-5e8f-b1f0-69426fcd72d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9f69be1a-7ddd-5b88-a4da-dc75ecb9eaff" :answer-field/choices ["answer-465105e6-5101-55c0-b1d1-06d1ae1a8a42" "answer-c6945ce8-db6b-5823-b2dc-01f0875bc633" "answer-8ea5fefa-7242-5713-8e02-211083d54f0a" "answer-9f69be1a-7ddd-5b88-a4da-dc75ecb9eaff" "answer-8434f6a8-cc90-5b45-b358-8909e66e4e5e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-465105e6-5101-55c0-b1d1-06d1ae1a8a42" :answer/id #uuid "465105e6-5101-55c0-b1d1-06d1ae1a8a42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6945ce8-db6b-5823-b2dc-01f0875bc633" :answer/id #uuid "c6945ce8-db6b-5823-b2dc-01f0875bc633" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ea5fefa-7242-5713-8e02-211083d54f0a" :answer/id #uuid "8ea5fefa-7242-5713-8e02-211083d54f0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f69be1a-7ddd-5b88-a4da-dc75ecb9eaff" :answer/id #uuid "9f69be1a-7ddd-5b88-a4da-dc75ecb9eaff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8434f6a8-cc90-5b45-b358-8909e66e4e5e" :answer/id #uuid "8434f6a8-cc90-5b45-b358-8909e66e4e5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1b5a0004-da97-5a43-bf86-5bd3413d5383" :question/id #uuid "1b5a0004-da97-5a43-bf86-5bd3413d5383" :question/math-academy-id "q-123639" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2}))}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})|\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}{[|-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})|]}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}(|-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})|-|-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})|) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4d754845-5d58-59c1-864c-f3740c76cc59"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4d754845-5d58-59c1-864c-f3740c76cc59" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d754845-5d58-59c1-864c-f3740c76cc59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-59a4d601-d2b3-5c64-9a6e-78d2d155f615" :answer-field/choices ["answer-acf332da-f102-5954-a0ff-4632294d19b6" "answer-48d38326-3827-5037-8c94-f55b16de2521" "answer-59a4d601-d2b3-5c64-9a6e-78d2d155f615" "answer-2b8f5946-803e-549c-a59d-30354b99ca23" "answer-5272c95e-f96d-52e0-9de8-9b6c1893b269"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-acf332da-f102-5954-a0ff-4632294d19b6" :answer/id #uuid "acf332da-f102-5954-a0ff-4632294d19b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48d38326-3827-5037-8c94-f55b16de2521" :answer/id #uuid "48d38326-3827-5037-8c94-f55b16de2521" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59a4d601-d2b3-5c64-9a6e-78d2d155f615" :answer/id #uuid "59a4d601-d2b3-5c64-9a6e-78d2d155f615" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b8f5946-803e-549c-a59d-30354b99ca23" :answer/id #uuid "2b8f5946-803e-549c-a59d-30354b99ca23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4-\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5272c95e-f96d-52e0-9de8-9b6c1893b269" :answer/id #uuid "5272c95e-f96d-52e0-9de8-9b6c1893b269" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6947d1ad-4cd9-585a-b94f-f141875b9f2d" :question/id #uuid "6947d1ad-4cd9-585a-b94f-f141875b9f2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-123581" :question/problem "![](images/36/36008a9155a01a07136cee263ce0a89239719227541536e8c2f8ea358d43e6df.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\cancel{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -\\cancel{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f262cbb1-b41b-5a16-a002-abeb999c9afc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f262cbb1-b41b-5a16-a002-abeb999c9afc" :answer-field/id #uuid "f262cbb1-b41b-5a16-a002-abeb999c9afc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cf8e5566-d63d-5c74-aea1-6e226a17823d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bfd8c063-a572-53c2-b4ce-461228304503" "answer-c9ae75cb-ec9f-5d2a-90c0-9d53665a6116" "answer-92d7287d-2c86-57db-807a-ce851e800dbe" "answer-cf8e5566-d63d-5c74-aea1-6e226a17823d" "answer-ad21357d-24c8-5905-9453-f8cf49c4c786"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfd8c063-a572-53c2-b4ce-461228304503" :answer/id #uuid "bfd8c063-a572-53c2-b4ce-461228304503" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9ae75cb-ec9f-5d2a-90c0-9d53665a6116" :answer/id #uuid "c9ae75cb-ec9f-5d2a-90c0-9d53665a6116" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92d7287d-2c86-57db-807a-ce851e800dbe" :answer/id #uuid "92d7287d-2c86-57db-807a-ce851e800dbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf8e5566-d63d-5c74-aea1-6e226a17823d" :answer/id #uuid "cf8e5566-d63d-5c74-aea1-6e226a17823d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad21357d-24c8-5905-9453-f8cf49c4c786" :answer/id #uuid "ad21357d-24c8-5905-9453-f8cf49c4c786" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-27eda322-b707-5345-adf8-0465217fdeaf" :question/id #uuid "27eda322-b707-5345-adf8-0465217fdeaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-149822" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path along the polar curve $r=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta $ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates, the arc length element $\\text{d}s$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSo, for a polar curve defined as $r=r(\\theta )$ for ${\\theta }_{1}\\le \\theta \\le {\\theta }_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $r=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta }=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we evaluate our line integral as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}\\sqrt{{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{(4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta )}^{2}+{(4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta )}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{16{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta +16{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta {tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{16{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta (1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{16{sec}^{4}⁡\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =4[\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-20dcdcfd-748c-52ae-895b-79a3d2f6200f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-20dcdcfd-748c-52ae-895b-79a3d2f6200f" :answer-field/id #uuid "20dcdcfd-748c-52ae-895b-79a3d2f6200f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9eeb0c86-cf6c-5ccc-baf9-def02136f813" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3155478e-1b5a-5e18-bd4c-26ed84959b1d" "answer-abcd435e-c198-5b6e-9039-b510adba1e54" "answer-8234212b-ceff-57f4-a7ce-844e2d396499" "answer-9eeb0c86-cf6c-5ccc-baf9-def02136f813" "answer-94931a58-c0c8-5c1d-bfbb-07691dddb8fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3155478e-1b5a-5e18-bd4c-26ed84959b1d" :answer/id #uuid "3155478e-1b5a-5e18-bd4c-26ed84959b1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abcd435e-c198-5b6e-9039-b510adba1e54" :answer/id #uuid "abcd435e-c198-5b6e-9039-b510adba1e54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8234212b-ceff-57f4-a7ce-844e2d396499" :answer/id #uuid "8234212b-ceff-57f4-a7ce-844e2d396499" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9eeb0c86-cf6c-5ccc-baf9-def02136f813" :answer/id #uuid "9eeb0c86-cf6c-5ccc-baf9-def02136f813" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94931a58-c0c8-5c1d-bfbb-07691dddb8fc" :answer/id #uuid "94931a58-c0c8-5c1d-bfbb-07691dddb8fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173201 :tutorial/content "Recall that for a path $C$ in the $xy$-plane, the arc length $L$ of $C$ can be computed as the line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nL = \\displaystyle\\int_C \\, \\textrm{d}s\n$$\n\nNow, if $C$ is defined parametrically as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle x(t),\\, y(t)\\rangle, \\quad a\\leq t \\leq b ,\n$$\n\nthen we can also calculate the arc length of $C$ as\n\n$$\nL = \\int_{a}^{b}||\\mathbf r'(t)||\\,\\textrm d t = \\int_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{\\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d t}\\right)^2}\\,\\textrm d t\\,.\n$$\n\nBy comparing our two expressions for $L,$ we say that the **arc-length element** $\\textrm ds$ for a parametrically defined curve is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm ds = \\sqrt{\\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d t}\\right)^2}\\,\\textrm d t\\,.\n$$\n\nGeometrically, we can think of $\\textrm ds$ as representing the change in arc length that arises due to a vanishingly small change in $t.$ By summing (integrating) all of these small changes, we arrive at the arc length of $C.$ We'll explore this in more detail at the end of the lesson." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173203 :tutorial/content "Let's now build up a geometric understanding of what the arc length element $\\textrm d s$ means. First, we'll consider the case of a parametric curve defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle x(t),\\, y(t)\\rangle.\n$$\n\nSuppose that the point $P$ lies on this curve and has position vector $\\mathbf r.$\n\n![](images/2b/2b302806eef01fd6e8160ee6e3183959537c0e9f5c6907238a2eea1d208d3da7.png)\n\nNow consider a small change $\\Delta t$ in the parameter $t.$ This change gives a new point $P'$ on the curve with position vector $\\mathbf r + \\Delta\\mathbf r,$ where $\\Delta \\mathbf r$ gives the total change (as a vector) in moving from $P$ to $P',$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/0b/0b1eb1dcc7be637e4e6024b5a8e9e13a4ea5c3e7439be7a2e3083f5ec274ef71.png)\n\nAccording to the diagram we have\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = x(t+\\Delta t) - x(t), \\qquad \\Delta y = y(t+\\Delta t) - y(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Delta x$ and $\\Delta y$ are the changes in $x$ and $y,$ respectively, corresponding to the change in $t.$\n\nUsing the fact that a difference quotient can be approximated as derivative, these quantities can be approximated as\n\n$$\n\\Delta x \\approx \\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}\\Delta t, \\qquad \\Delta y \\approx \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d t}\\Delta t.\n$$\n\nThe change in arc length $\\Delta s$ can be approximated as the magnitude of $\\Delta \\mathbf r.$ Therefore, by the Pythagorean theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(Δs)^{2} & ≈||Δr|{|}^{2} \\\\  & ={(Δx)}^{2}+{(Δy)}^{2} \\\\  & ≈{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}Δt)}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}Δt)}^{2} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}(Δt)^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}(Δt)^{2} \\\\  & =[{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}](Δt)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\Delta s\n\n\\approx\n\n\\sqrt{\\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}\\right)^2  + \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d t}\\right)^2}\\, \\Delta t.\n$$\n\nIf we imagine the limiting case where $\\Delta t \\to 0,$ we arrive at the arc length element $\\textrm d s\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\textrm d s\n\n=\n\n\\sqrt{\\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}\\right)^2  + \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d t}\\right)^2}\\, \\textrm d t\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173204 :tutorial/content "Now, let's derive the formula for the arc length element $\\textrm d s$ for a curve defined using plane polar coordinates. We will use a similar geometric approach.\n\nConsider a curve $r= r(\\theta)$ defined using polar coordinates. Suppose that the point $P$ lies on this curve and has position vector $\\mathbf r.$\n\n![](images/7f/7fa77b8d4ad159967f917b438096f472cbd7f541495847e11b919a6843e6259b.png)\n\nNow consider a small change $\\Delta \\theta$ in the parameter $\\theta.$ This change gives a new point $P'$ on the curve with position vector $\\mathbf r + \\Delta\\mathbf r,$ where $\\Delta \\mathbf r$ gives the total change (as a vector) in moving from $P$ to $P',$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/10/105112a2bb993a13282c5f36190ca99a46d80a22a4203f653f7f67060e486d48.png)\n\nFrom here, we see that the vector $\\Delta \\mathbf r$ can be approximated as the vector addition of two components:\n\n- a vector of length $\\Delta r$ acting parallel to $\\mathbf r,$ and\n\n- a vector of length $r\\Delta \\theta$ acting perpendicular to $\\mathbf r.$\n\n![](images/08/080fa1112410328ba369e1c2e5d70fc2e5ddba97606a2fdeaa90d61e3e20d874.png)\n\nNote that $\\Delta r$ is simply the difference of the radial lengths between the points $P$ and $P'.$ The expression $r\\Delta \\theta$ comes from the formula for the arc length of a sector of a circle.\n\nNow, the change in arc length $\\Delta s$ can be approximated as the magnitude of $\\Delta \\mathbf r.$ Since our two components are perpendicular, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(Δs)^{2} & ≈||Δr|{|}^{2} \\\\  & ≈(Δr)^{2}+(rΔ\\theta )^{2} \\\\  & =Δ{r}^{2}+{r}^{2}(Δ\\theta )^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that a difference quotient can be approximated as derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\Delta r = r(\\theta + \\Delta\\theta) - r(\\theta) = \\dfrac{\\textrm d r}{\\textrm d \\theta}\\Delta\\theta.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our expression for $(\\Delta s)^2$ above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(Δs)^{2} & ≈{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}(Δ\\theta )^{2}+{r}^{2}(Δ\\theta )^{2} \\\\  & ={r}^{2}(Δ\\theta )^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}(Δ\\theta )^{2} \\\\  & =[{r}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}\\theta })}^{2}](Δ\\theta )^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\Delta s = \\sqrt{r^2 + \\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm d r}{\\textrm d \\theta}\\right)^2}\\Delta\\theta.\n$$\n\nIf we imagine the limiting case where $\\Delta \\theta \\to 0,$ we arrive at the arc length element $\\textrm d s\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\textrm d s\n\n=\n\n\\sqrt{r^2 + \\left(\\dfrac{\\textrm d r}{\\textrm d \\theta}\\right)^2}\\textrm d\\theta\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172176 :activity/expected-seconds 540.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
